@startuml
title Idempotency Lifecycle

hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

state "ABSENT" as ABSENT
state "PROCESSING\nowner + version\nprocessingExpireAt" as PROCESSING
state "SUCCESS\noptional result payload" as SUCCESS
state "FAILED\nfailureRetryable" as FAILED

[*] --> ABSENT
ABSENT --> PROCESSING : tryAcquire ACQUIRED\nowner=A version=1

PROCESSING --> SUCCESS : current owner markSuccess\nCAS owner/version
PROCESSING --> FAILED : current owner markFailed\nCAS owner/version

PROCESSING --> PROCESSING : duplicate while active\nRETURN PROCESSING
PROCESSING --> PROCESSING : normal execute after timeout\nRETURN PROCESSING_EXPIRED\n(no state change)

PROCESSING --> PROCESSING : recover timeout allowed\nCAS expected A/10\nnew B/11
FAILED --> PROCESSING : recover retryable allowed\nCAS expected A/10\nnew B/11

SUCCESS --> SUCCESS : duplicate\nREPLAY
FAILED --> FAILED : normal execute\nRETURN previous failure

SUCCESS --> PROCESSING : WINDOWED semantic window expired\nnext execute starts version+1
FAILED --> PROCESSING : WINDOWED semantic window expired\nnext execute starts version+1

note right of PROCESSING
PROCESSING_ACTIVE / PROCESSING_EXPIRED
are derived decisions, not persisted statuses.

Any stale markSuccess/markFailed with an old
owner/version must update 0 rows / be rejected.
end note

note bottom of SUCCESS
DURABLE: long-lived business fact.
WINDOWED: when windowExpireAt is reached,
a new generation may start even if physical
record is still retained.
end note
@enduml
